+// The runoff-v1 optics are expressed in logical pixels. Keep this bound in sync with the shader.
+// A runoff lane has |dx| <= 23. Its two lenses contribute <= 2 * 2.46 * 23
+// per unit coverage, and its film contributes <= (0.72 / 0.64) * 23.
+// In Y, the two unmerged head tests bound the contribution by 6.68 * size + 6.40.
+// In a merger, the larger signed lens distance is at most aa + 1.25 * neck;
+// neck <= 0.625 * min(rx), ry <= 1.147 * size, rx <= 1.185 * size, and ry/min(rx,ry) <= 5.
+// With contour <= 1.4 and lens strength <= 2.46, this gives 7.15 * size + 11.20.
+// The outer join interpolates toward each contribution per unit of its coverage,
+// so it preserves the largest bound. Beads and drainage have smaller bounds.
+// Round up and include the half-pixel UV inset and floating-point slack.
+fn rain_refraction_bound(size: f64) -> [f64; 2] {
+    [144.0, 8.0 * size + 16.0]
+}
